-- ============================================================
-- Psych/Soc: vocabulary seed and card mapping
--
-- APPROVED after a granularity and discipline QA. 239 new CONTENT concepts
-- and a PRIMARY mapping for all 778 Psych/Soc flashcards. No REASONING and no
-- QUANTITATIVE objects: the cards teach bias vocabulary as definitions to
-- recall, not as operations applied to evidence, and no card teaches generic
-- statistics.
--
-- THE CORRECTION THIS PHASE RESTS ON. The first design forced all 268 proposed
-- concepts into Psychology or Sociology because the cards sit in the Psych/Soc
-- curriculum. That is the section, not the discipline. 62 concepts now involve
-- BIOLOGY: 59 as Psychology-primary biological psychology, and 3 where neither
-- Psychology nor Sociology is intrinsic to the objective at all. All 239 sit in
-- the PSYCH_SOC section regardless, because that is where the MCAT examines
-- them. Section and discipline disagreeing is the correct outcome here.
--
-- GRANULARITY. The QA merged 30 concepts and split one, taking 268 to 239 and
-- single-card concepts from 72 to 42. One merge fixed a genuine duplicate:
-- Parkinson's disease was taught by two concepts in two different decks.
--
-- PROVENANCE. Every card mapping is AI_PROPOSED. The vocabulary was approved;
-- 778 individual rows were not reviewed one by one.
--
-- WRITE SCOPE. Concepts, their taxonomy, and flashcard_concepts. No learner
-- table is read or written.
-- ============================================================

BEGIN;

